  the fit is the headline of the lane: Delta_req = A s^p with p = 0.811 +/- 0.079 and A = 5.47 +/- 0.83.
  Since g_phi = a0 Delta = A a0^(1-p) g_N^p, p = 1 makes a0 CANCEL: the requirement would then be g_phi = A g_N, a constant
  rescaling of G by 1+A -- extra MASS tracing the baryons, not an interpolation function with an acceleration scale.
  [PASS] C2 [function] the required Delta_req is single-valued in s to better than 0.30 dex: a necessary condition for ANY kernel Delta(s) of the class to reproduce clusters   (pooled within-bin rms across clusters = 0.147 dex (all bins, both footings, both subsets))
  [PASS] C3 [stiffness] the required Delta_req is non-decreasing in s, so the longitudinal stiffness dg_N/dg_phi = 1/Delta'(s) stays positive and the static field problem stays well posed   (canonical/all worst step +1.30 sigma; canonical/stellar worst step +1.11 sigma; alt/all worst step +1.22 sigma; alt/stellar worst step +1.10 sigma)
  [FAIL] C4 [bounded] the required Delta_req respects the bounded-boost ceiling of the kernel family, so some interpolation function of the class can supply it   (max required Delta = 3.01 (headline stellar-7 canonical 2.94) against the widest ceiling C_max = 1.000: over by 3.0x)

