  [FAIL] C9 [shape] the required Delta_req has the log-slope of a kernel of the class: the fitted p is not more than 3 sigma above the class ceiling of 1/2 (a p near 1 instead means g_phi = A g_N with a0 cancelling -- a constant rescaling of G, i.e. extra mass tracing the baryons, not an interpolation function)   (family max log-slope over the cluster range = 0.427; required canonical/all p = 0.726 +/- 0.068 (+3.3 sigma above 1/2), canonical/stellar p = 0.811 +/- 0.079 (+3.9 sigma above 1/2), alt/all p = 0.726 +/- 0.068 (+3.3 sigma above 1/2), alt/stellar p = 0.811 +/- 0.078 (+4.0 sigma above 1/2))

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  THE ANSWER TO THE INVERSE PROBLEM, in one place.
  Over the acceleration range clusters probe, s = g_bar/a0 in [0.09, 0.91], the boost that reproduces the corrected
  X-COP enclosed-mass profile exactly from the baryons alone is  Delta_req(s) = (5.5 +/- 0.8) s^(0.81 +/- 0.08)  (rms 0.09 dex,
  seven clusters with measured stellar profiles, canonical footing; the alt footing returns the SAME exponent and A smaller
  by 3.5%, since Delta a0 and s a0 are both measured accelerations and only the p != 1 residual sees the footing).  Equivalently J_Y = s/Delta_req = 0.126-0.184 over that range: nearly a
  CONSTANT, i.e. G rescaled by 1/J_Y ~ 6.9.  It is single-valued (C2) and monotone (C3) -- so as a mathematical object it exists --
  but it is 2.9x above the widest ceiling any kernel of the class can reach (C4), it is 4.0x the boost galaxies MEASURE at the
  same accelerations (C5, worst |z| = 13), and its monotone continuation is 4e+04x the Saturn residual bound (C6).
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  caveats: the cluster side inherits every caveat of the lead's audit (hydrostatic equilibrium, the FORW mass
  reconstruction, sphericity, tabulated central profiles, no covariance) and the five clusters without a measured
  stellar profile have gas-only baryons, which is why the seven-cluster subset carries the headline; the galaxy side
  uses SPARC's fixed Upsilon at 3.6um, so a coherent stellar-normalisation shift moves Delta_galaxy, but the
  Newtonian limit pins the coherent part to a few per cent (PAPER5) and the cluster/galaxy ratio here is far larger.
  The inversion itself assumes only spherical symmetry and the programme's own static law; it is exact given those.
  total 3s

